      "extract": "For a positive integer n, the n-colored Jones polynomial is a Laurent polyno- mial invariant in q of a knot colored with n-dimensional irreducible representation of Uq(sl2). We denote by JK(n) the n-colored Jones polynomial of a knot K, which is normalized so that the colored Jones polynomial of the trivial knot is 1. Then, JK(2) coincides with the original Jones polynomial of a knot K deﬁned by V. F. R. Jones [3].",
      "extractCut": true
